--------------------------

OpenRGB
  License: GPL-2.0
  Used as: an external program / SDK server reached over a TCP socket (arm's-length
           communication). OpenRGB's source is NOT copied, linked, or bundled here.
  Bundled: NO. Install OpenRGB yourself (https://openrgb.org/).

openrgb-python (jath03/openrgb-python)
  License: GPL-3.0
  Used as: a Python client library imported by station/agent-lightsd.py
           (`from openrgb import OpenRGBClient`).
  IMPORTANT: importing a GPL-3.0 library is an argument for linking / a derivative
  work. As shipped, the daemon module effectively carries GPL-3.0 obligations when
  distributed together with openrgb-python, even though the rest of the original code
  in this repository is offered under MIT. This library is NOT bundled here; it is a
  declared dependency you install separately.
  Planned: replace this client with a from-scratch implementation of the OpenRGB SDK
  wire protocol over a raw socket, so the daemon can be pure MIT with no GPL client.
  Until then, treat station/agent-lightsd.py as GPL-3.0-encumbered when used with
  openrgb-python.

